        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: മയങ്ങുക",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മയങ്ങുക — mayaṅṅuka — \"to doze off; to drowse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഊണ് കഴിഞ്ഞ് മുത്തശ്ശി കസേരയിൽ ഇരുന്ന് മയങ്ങി. ūṇŭ kaḻiññŭ muttaśśi kasērayil irunnŭ mayaṅṅi. After lunch grandmother dozed off in her chair."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past: മയങ്ങി, mayaṅṅi."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A light sleep; the noun is മയക്കം, drowsiness, as after a meal or a medicine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മയങ്ങുക (mayaṅṅuka) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4706 gives it as to be drowsy or giddy, with മയക്കം, drowsiness (DEDR 4706)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
